nd Qasimis turned to Sunni Islam: “The expansion of the Qasimi state into Sunni areas led to unprecedented levels of interaction between Zaydi and Shafi\'i scholars. The effect was that Zaydis acquired greater awarness of the wider Sunni world and began studying Sunni works, namely the collections of hadlth, with an intensity never before seen, and some even adopted Sunni views.”  “In the words of one of Husayn al-Huthi\'s peers, ‘especially under the rule of the Qasimi imams, the Zaydis had become more Sunni than\xa0ahl al-bayt’ (here: neglecting the legacy of the Prophet\'s House).” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 983, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 843})
