usading was the reign, and later the canonisation, of Louis IX, the saint-king – who in his turn became a key figure in the political theology of Philip IV. In Louis’s name Philip was to humble the papacy and suppress the Templars because in his eyes they stood in the way of the Capetian monarchy, acting on God’s behalf.”'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 896, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 774})
