mins, devoted to their studies and religious duties, held a high position in society.”  “A temple of the Hindu deities Minakshi and Sundareshvara (Parvati and Shiva), located at Madurai in Tamil Nadu. It was initially built by the Pandya dynasty, and reconstructed in the seventeenth century, during the time of the Nayaka dynasty. This elaborate temple complex actually has two temples, one dedicated to Shiva as Sndareshvara, the other to Minakshi.”  “Pandyan courtly epics extol Madurai as a city of extreme beauty, and connect the Pandya royal lineage with Minakshi, the tutelary goddess of Madurai, and her consort, Sundareshvara (a form of Shiva).” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 999, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 833})
